<title>CYPRUS: SOCCER-GOGIC DOUBLE SINKS ISRAEL.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GOGIC DOUBLE SINKS ISRAEL.</headline>
<dateline>LIMASSOL, Cyprus 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinica Gogic's double strike in the opening 15 minutes was enough to give Cyprus a 2-0 World Cup qualifying win over Israel on Sunday.</p>
<p>He headed home the first in the ninth minute from a cross from the right by Marios Christodoulou.</p>
<p>Six minutes later he was felled by goalkeeper Rafi Cohen and converted the penalty himself.</p>
<p>Israel were unlucky in the 75th minute when Alon Hazan's shot hit the post.</p>
<p>The defeat left them three points behind group five leaders Russia.</p>
</text>
